{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"56","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Spoilt Permutation"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya collects coins: he has exactly one coin for every year from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". Naturally, Vasya keeps all the coins in his collection in the order in which they were released. Once Vasya's younger brother made a change — he took all the coins whose release year dated from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" inclusively and put them in the reverse order. That is, he took a certain segment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[l, r]"},{"kind":"text","text":" and reversed it. At that the segment's endpoints did not coincide. For example, if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n = 8"},{"kind":"text","text":", then initially Vasya's coins were kept in the order "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". If Vasya's younger brother chose the segment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[2, 6]"},{"kind":"text","text":", then after the reversal the coin order will change to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 6 5 4 3 2 7 8"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Vasya suspects that someone else could have spoilt the permutation after his brother. Help him to find that out. Check if the given permutation can be obtained from the permutation "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 2 ... "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" using exactly one segment reversal. If it is possible, find the segment itself."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 1000"},{"kind":"text","text":") which is the number of coins in Vasya's collection. The second line contains space-separated "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers which are the spoilt sequence of coins. It is guaranteed that the given sequence is a permutation, i.e. it contains only integers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", and every number is used exactly 1 time."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is impossible to obtain the given permutation from the original one in exactly one action, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0 0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Otherwise, print two numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ l < r ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") which are the endpoints of the segment that needs to be reversed to obtain from permutation "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 2 ... "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the given one."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8\n1 6 5 4 3 2 7 8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n2 3 4 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n1 2 3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"56B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/56/problem/B"}